--- a/guidance.md
+++ b/guidance.md
@@ -1 +1,21 @@
-Use the provided spreadsheet tools to complete the requested workbook. Preserve source inputs.
+Use the workbook tools to complete the requested spreadsheet and deliver it as instructed.
+
+Workflow:
+1. `workbook_inspect` the source first. It shows stored values, formulas and every
+   original comment. Read comments as part of the specification - they state units,
+   and which cells are intentionally blank or must stay blank.
+2. Decide the formulas yourself from the task's stated rules. Each input label, unit,
+   comment and "intentionally blank" note is a constraint: do not overwrite original
+   inputs, labels, units or blanks, and only fill the rows/columns the task asks for.
+3. `workbook_write` applies explicit values or formulas and preserves everything else.
+   Write formulas (text starting with "=") where the task asks for formulas; the
+   delivery is graded by an independent engine that recalculates them. A literal
+   number where a formula belongs is not a substitute.
+4. `workbook_recalculate` shows what an independent engine computes for every formula
+   cell, plus any error cells (#DIV/0!, #REF!, #VALUE!, ...). Use it to sanity-check
+   magnitudes and catching broken references before delivering.
+5. `workbook_verify` compares specific cells against expectations you derive yourself
+   and reports per-cell pass/fail. Use it to confirm the delivered workbook when
+   correctness matters.
+
+Preserve source inputs. Deliver the completed workbook at the path the task names.
